<BaseLayout
  title="Research Methodology"
  description="How Greek Invest researches Greek property: the four checks every page passes, the sources we prioritise, how figures are dated, and our referral policy."
>
  <section class="site-container py-12 md:py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="mb-6">Methodology</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Every page on this site is written against primary Greek sources and checked before publication.
        This page sets out exactly what those checks are, where the numbers come from, and what we do
        when the law changes, so that any figure you read here can be traced rather than trusted.
      </p>

      <h2>The four checks every page passes</h2>
      <p>Greek property content fails in four predictable places. We check each one before publishing:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>The correct Law 5100/2024 tier for the cadastral parcel.</strong> The €800,000 and
          €400,000 thresholds follow the regional unit on the cadastral extract, not the postcode or
          the marketing address. A scheme advertised as one municipality can sit in another.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>120 m² of main usable area on the engineer's certificate.</strong> The rule counts
          κύρια χρήση recorded on the Electronic Building Identity, never the floor plan or the
          listing. Balconies, parking and storage are excluded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A single title deed.</strong> Two adjoining properties do not combine to reach a
          threshold unless they are legally merged into one horizontal property first.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Traceable transfer of funds under Circular 1/2026.</strong> The purchase price must
          arrive from abroad through a Greek credit institution, into an account in the buyer's own name.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Sources we prioritise</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Greek legislation as published in the Government Gazette, and AADE circulars</li>
        <li>Ministry of Migration and Asylum statistics on residence permits</li>
        <li>Bank of Greece residential property indices and ELSTAT data</li>
        <li>Land Registry and Hellenic Cadastre transaction records</li>
        <li>Licensed Greek lawyers, notaries and civil engineers, clearly labelled as third-party</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Where we cite a market price rather than an official statistic, it is an asking-price range from
        portals and agencies, labelled as such, because asking prices lead the market and official indices
        lag it. Neither is the state's objective value, which is what transfer tax is actually charged on.
      </p>

      <h2>How figures are dated</h2>
      <p>
        Greek thresholds, tax bands and transfer rules change, sometimes twice in a year. Every material
        figure carries the date it was verified, and each guide shows an <em>Updated</em> date when the
        facts behind it move. Our two dataset pages, Golden Visa statistics and the regional price index,
        state their own quarterly update cadence. Always confirm numbers with your own lawyer and with
        AADE before signing anything.
      </p>

      <h2>What we are, and are not</h2>
      <p>
        Greek Invest is an independent editorial resource. We are not a developer, a law firm or a licensed
        Greek broker, and we are not paid by developers for editorial placement. Project reviews are written
        from public developer material and independent checks, and say so.
      </p>

      <h2>Referral policy</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit the shortlist or consultation form, your enquiry may be shared with
        <strong>licensed Greek lawyers and partner agents</strong> who can carry out regulated work we
        cannot: title searches, engineer certificates, notarial deeds and the Ministry file. We do not sell
        your data or pass it to unrelated marketing lists. See the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
